<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  The same exclusions for API 30 and below, which uses the older format.
  Both attributes are needed on the application tag: apps targeting Android
  12+ still run on older releases, and each version reads only its own file.

  Keep this list identical to backup_rules.xml. It drifted once, on August 14,
  2026: the queue exclusion was added there and not here, so on API 26 through
  30 (which minSdk still admits) the encrypted queue kept riding cloud backup
  while the newer file said it did not. Two files stating one policy is exactly
  the shape of thing that goes stale, and the only defence is remembering that
  this one exists.

  Note what the exclusion does and does not buy. It never saves the captures:
  the Keystore key does not travel either, so a restored queue is unreadable on
  the new device whichever file is in force. What it buys is keeping somebody's
  unfiltered thinking off a backup server at all, which is the half that was
  missing here.

  Note for anyone editing: XML comments may not contain a double hyphen, so
  this file cannot use the dashes the rest of the codebase writes with. The
  same warning is in backup_rules.xml, and writing this file without carrying
  it over is how the build broke while making this very change.
-->
<full-backup-content>
    <exclude domain="sharedpref" path="clarice_capture_secret.xml" />
    <exclude domain="sharedpref" path="second_mind_capture_secret.xml" />
    <exclude domain="sharedpref" path="clarice_capture_queue_store.xml" />
</full-backup-content>
